  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene of environmental pollution",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual and textual elements of the meme, which collectively depict a scene of severe environmental pollution. The text 'so much trash' and 'we need a garbage collector' implicitly address the viewer, inviting them to recognize the problem and consider their role in or responsibility for the waste crisis. The overwhelming visual of the trash pile serves as a direct projection of the user's potential complicity or concern for the global waste crisis. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the imperative tone of 'we need a garbage collector' and the visual shock of the scene create an implicit projection of the user as part of the collective facing this environmental issue.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
